<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fritz Steinbach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1855–1916</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fritz Steinbach was a German conductor and composer. As director of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiningen">Meiningen</a> court orchestra from 1886 to 1903 he became one of the most admired interpreters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-brahms">Johannes Brahms</a>, who approved his performances of the symphonies. He later led the Gürzenich Orchestra and the conservatory in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, and his markings of Brahms's scores influenced later conductors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fritz-steinbach.jpg" alt="Fritz Steinbach" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Eduard Klamroth · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FritzSteinbach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
